\1\n    <div id="site-header"></div>
    <!-- Header -->
    
    <main class="lesson-container py-4">
        <!-- Breadcrumb -->
        <div id="tutorial-header"></div>
        
        <div class="content lesson-content" style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-secondary);">
            <p>IP addresses are split into public and private ranges to conserve addresses and improve security.</p><h3>Private IP Address</h3><p>Used inside your LAN. It is not routable on the internet. Common ranges are <code>192.168.x.x</code> or <code>10.x.x.x</code>.</p><h3>Public IP Address</h3><p>Assigned by your ISP to your router. This is the address the internet sees. Your router uses NAT (Network Address Translation) to translate between your private devices and the single public IP.</p>
        </div>
        
